---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/page/PageHero.astro';
import Band from '../components/ui/Band.astro';
import Prose from '../components/page/Prose.astro';
import { staticRow, org, editorialFor } from '../lib/page.js';

const ed = editorialFor('terms');
const row = staticRow({
  path: '/terms',
  pageType: 'core',
  title: ed.metaTitle ?? 'Terms of Service | MrMoverPacker',
  h1: ed.title ?? 'Terms of service',
  metaDescription:
    ed.seoDescription ??
    'The terms for quotes, bookings, payments, cancellations, liability and claims when you move with MrMoverPacker, written in plain language.',
  breadcrumbs: [{ path: '/', anchor: 'Home' }],
});
const o = org();
const legalName = o?.legalName ?? 'MR MOVER PACKER';
const brand = o?.brandName ?? 'MrMoverPacker';
---

<BaseLayout row={row}>
  <PageHero
    dark
    eyebrow={ed.eyebrow ?? 'Legal'}
    h1={row.h1}
    intro={ed.intro ??
      'The plain-language terms for using our website and moving services. We’ve kept them readable on purpose. You shouldn’t need a lawyer to understand what you’re agreeing to.'}
    breadcrumbs={row.breadcrumbs}
    current="Terms"
  />

  <Band label="Terms">
    <Prose>
      {
        ed.bodyHtml ? (
          <Fragment set:html={ed.bodyHtml} />
        ) : (
          <Fragment>
            <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: 17 October 2026</p>

            <h2>1. Who these terms are with</h2>
            <p>
              These terms are an agreement between you and <strong>{legalName}</strong>, trading as{' '}
              {brand}, a GST-registered business in India ("we", "us"). They apply when you use this
              website, ask for a quote, or book a move with us. Your written quote forms part of
              these terms; where the two differ, the quote wins for your move.
            </p>

            <h2>2. What we do</h2>
            <p>
              We pack, load, move, unload and unpack household and office goods, and transport cars
              and bikes, for customers in the areas we serve. We have no walk-in branches: our crews
              come to you, and everything else is handled by phone, WhatsApp and email.
            </p>

            <h2>3. Estimates, surveys and your written quote</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>
                Any price shown on this website, including the instant price check, is an estimate
                for guidance. It is not an offer or a quote.
              </li>
              <li>
                Your quote is prepared after a survey of your goods, in person or by video, and sent
                to you in writing. It is fixed for the goods, addresses, floors, access, services
                and date it describes.
              </li>
              <li>
                A quote is valid for the period printed on it. After that, or if the details you
                gave were not accurate, we may need to re-quote.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <h2>4. What can change the price</h2>
            <p>
              The quoted price changes only if the job changes. We tell you the extra cost and get
              your agreement before doing the extra work. Typical reasons:
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li>Goods added that were not in the survey, or an extra pickup or drop point.</li>
              <li>Floors, stairs or a missing lift that were not declared.</li>
              <li>A carry of more than 50 metres between your door and the truck.</li>
              <li>
                Waiting beyond the agreed time because the site, keys or permissions were not ready.
              </li>
              <li>A change of date, time or address after booking.</li>
              <li>
                Society, parking, lift or entry charges, tolls and government levies that were not
                in the quote. These are charged at actual cost, with the receipt where there is one.
              </li>
              <li>Crating, dismantling or other services you ask for on the day.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>5. Booking and payment</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>
                Your booking is confirmed when you accept the written quote and pay the token
                advance shown on it.
              </li>
              <li>
                The balance is due on completion of the move, unless your quote says otherwise. We
                accept UPI, bank transfer and the other methods named on your quote.
              </li>
              <li>
                GST is charged as applicable and shown separately. You receive a GST invoice for
                every move.
              </li>
              <li>
                We may hold your goods until the agreed charges are paid. We will always tell you
                first and try to settle any dispute about charges quickly.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <h2>6. Cancelling or rescheduling</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>
                Cancel or reschedule at least 48 hours before the pickup time and your token advance
                is refunded in full, or moved to the new date.
              </li>
              <li>
                Inside 48 hours, we may keep a cancellation fee, as printed on your quote, to cover
                the crew, vehicle and materials already set aside for you. The rest is refunded.
              </li>
              <li>Refunds are paid to your original payment method within 7 working days.</li>
              <li>
                If we have to cancel, for safety, legal or other reasons outside your control, we
                refund everything you paid or move your booking to a date that suits you.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <h2>7. What we need from you</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>Accurate details of your goods, addresses, floors and access.</li>
              <li>
                Society, building and lift permissions, and a place for the truck to stand, unless
                we agreed to arrange them.
              </li>
              <li>
                You, or someone you name, present at pickup and delivery to check the inventory and
                sign for it.
              </li>
              <li>
                Appliances switched off, defrosted, drained and disconnected, unless disconnection
                is in your quote.
              </li>
              <li>
                Cash, jewellery, documents, medicines, data and other valuables carried by you, not
                packed with your goods.
              </li>
              <li>That you own the goods, or have the right to move them.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>8. Goods we cannot move</h2>
            <p>
              For safety and legal reasons we do not carry: cash, jewellery and precious items;
              explosives and fireworks; gas cylinders that are not empty; petrol, diesel, kerosene
              and other flammable liquids; acids, chemicals and battery acid; firearms and
              ammunition; drugs and anything illegal; perishable food; and pets. Plants are carried
              only at your risk. If such goods are found among your things, we may refuse to carry
              them, and you are responsible for any loss or penalty they cause.
            </p>

            <h2>9. Packing</h2>
            <p>
              We are responsible for what our crew packs. Cartons you pack yourself are carried as
              they are: we cannot answer for damage inside a carton we did not pack or inspect,
              unless the carton itself was damaged in our care.
            </p>

            <h2>10. Our liability</h2>
            <p>
              We are responsible for loss of, or damage to, your goods caused while they are in our
              care. Your quote shows the basic liability cover included with your move, and the
              option of transit insurance up to the value you declare. Without transit insurance,
              what we pay for a loss or damage is limited to that basic cover.
            </p>
            <p>We are not responsible for:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Damage or wear that was there before the move, as recorded in the inventory.</li>
              <li>
                The working of electrical, electronic or mechanical items, unless they were visibly
                damaged in our care.
              </li>
              <li>Goods in cartons you packed yourself (section 9).</li>
              <li>
                Loss or delay caused by events outside our reasonable control, such as floods,
                storms, fire, riots, strikes, road closures, accidents caused by others, or
                government action.
              </li>
              <li>Indirect losses, such as lost earnings, hotel bills or missed appointments.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              Nothing in these terms limits your rights under the Consumer Protection Act, 2019, or
              any other law that cannot be excluded by agreement.
            </p>

            <h2>11. Claims</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>
                Check your goods at delivery. Note any visible damage or missing item on the
                delivery inventory before you sign it, and photograph it.
              </li>
              <li>
                Damage you find later, on unpacking, must be reported in writing within 6 days of
                delivery, or within the longer window printed on your invoice.
              </li>
              <li>
                Keep the item and its packing until the claim is closed, and let us inspect it.
              </li>
              <li>
                Claims are checked against the photo inventory signed at pickup and settled as
                described on our <a href="/claims">claims page</a>.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <h2>12. Transit insurance</h2>
            <p>
              Transit insurance is optional and is shown on your quote as its own line, priced
              against the value you declare. When you take it, the policy and its terms decide what
              is covered and how a claim under it is paid, and we help you make the claim. See our{' '}
              <a href="/insurance">insurance page</a>.
            </p>

            <h2>13. Cars and bikes</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>
                At pickup we photograph the vehicle with you and note its condition, odometer and
                fuel. Claims are assessed against that record.
              </li>
              <li>
                Hand over a copy of the RC and the insurance, and keep the fuel low. Remove personal
                belongings and loose accessories: they are not covered inside the vehicle.
              </li>
              <li>
                We are responsible for visible damage that happens in our care. Mechanical,
                electrical and battery faults are not covered.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <h2>14. Storage</h2>
            <p>
              If we store your goods, the charges, period and terms are agreed in writing before
              storage starts.
            </p>

            <h2>15. Delivery times</h2>
            <p>
              Your quote gives a delivery date or window. It is our honest estimate, and we work to
              meet it, but traffic, weather, road or permit checks and other events outside our
              control can delay a move. If that happens we keep you informed.
            </p>

            <h2>16. Contacting you</h2>
            <p>
              When you send a form, request a call or chat with us, you agree that we may call, text
              or WhatsApp you about your move. We do not send you marketing without your consent.
              How we handle your details is set out in our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
            </p>

            <h2>17. Using this website</h2>
            <p>
              We work to keep this website accurate and available, but it is provided as it is, and
              estimates on it are not quotes. Its content, name, logo and design belong to us and
              may not be copied or used to pass yourself off as us. Please do not misuse the site,
              for example by scraping it or trying to break its security. Report anyone pretending
              to be us through our <a href="/fraud-check">fraud-check page</a>.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Your account.</strong> You can create a free account to see your quotes and
              moves and save your addresses. Please use your own mobile number and correct details,
              keep your password to yourself, and tell us straight away if you think someone else
              has used your account. We may suspend or close an account that is misused or set up
              with someone else's number. You can ask us to close yours at any time; how we handle
              its data is in our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
            </p>

            <h2>18. Complaints and disputes</h2>
            <p>
              If something goes wrong, tell us first through our{' '}
              <a href="/raise-a-complaint">complaints page</a>. We aim to settle every complaint
              within 30 days. These terms are governed by the laws of India. Any dispute is subject
              to the courts at our principal place of business, without affecting your right to
              approach a consumer commission.
            </p>

            <h2>19. Changes to these terms</h2>
            <p>
              We may update these terms. The version on this page on the day you accept your quote
              applies to your move.
            </p>

            <h2>20. Contact</h2>
            <p>
              Questions about these terms? Reach us through the{' '}
              <a href="/company/contact">contact page</a>.
            </p>
          </Fragment>
        )
      }
    </Prose>
  </Band>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-updated {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-ink-500);
  }
</style>
